learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-10T18:52:02.925Z","harness:codex","Persist digest algorithm per record, keep absent labels permanently SHA256, and preserve each retained checkpoint hash epoch during compaction. Exported proof digests commit to exact stream bytes, so maintenance requires a new independently retained proof."
  "2026-09-10T21:41:09.249Z","harness:codex","Validate the complete retained evidence list before accepting reduced proof coverage. A valid digest-only or legacy anchor result may limit reconstruction, but it must never hide invalid metadata in earlier evidence. New audit events use the current writer default; preserving historical algorithm commitments does not imply a sticky stream-tail writer policy."
